// Shared chrome for every overlay window: the borderless/always-on-top
// window flags common to all of them.
//
// Deliberately doesn't also declare the `locked`/`force-show`/
// `drag-requested` contract each overlay's own drag TouchArea uses, even
// though that trio is just as duplicated: slint_build's generated Rust API
// for a component only exposes accessors (`set_locked`, `on_drag_requested`,
// ...) for properties/callbacks declared directly on that component, not
// ones it merely inherits from a base in another file — so those three
// still have to be redeclared in each leaf `.slint` file for
// `AlertOverlayWindow`/`HistoryOverlayWindow`/`DpsMeterWindow`'s Rust side
// to see them. `no-frame`/`background`/`always-on-top` aren't `in`
// properties and need no Rust accessor, so those are safe to share here.
//
// Also doesn't own the drag TouchArea itself: each overlay places its drag
// catcher at a different point in its own element tree (a top-level sibling
// covering the alert overlay's transparent canvas; the first child of
// `panel` for history/DPS's opaque panel, so their later-declared
// interactive rows/tabs/buttons still take priority over it for clicks in
// their own bounds). Hoisting the TouchArea here would force one placement
// on every overlay or need a `@children` injection point — not worth the
// risk to DPS's mob-picker/tab click layering for a few lines of markup.
export component OverlayShell inherits Window {
    no-frame: true;
    background: transparent;
    always-on-top: true;
}
